  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Skinning in the open world keeps the authored requirement with level scaling on and off",
  "contract": "Requires DestinyWeaver.Enable=1, DestinyWeaver.LevelScaling=1 and DestinyWeaver.Scaling.Offset=3. Spell::CheckCast requires (level - 10) * 10 Skinning below 100 skill, so a level-20 Ranger with Skinning 40 skins beasts of level 5 (0), 11 (10) and 14 (40, the orange edge) and is refused SPELL_FAILED_LOW_CASTLEVEL (49) by level 15 (50). In the open world the Destiny Weaver only lifts a creature, to 17 for a level-20 character. The lift must not raise the skinning requirement: the corpse's skinning loot is the authored creature's, and a lifted requirement would lock a scaled character out of every beast below its own level (a level-5 wolf shown at 17 needs 70). With scaling off the same four beasts give the same four results. Black Riding Wolf 5194 is a beast with skinning table 100001 and no creature loot or money, so its corpse becomes skinnable as soon as it dies.",
